# A narrow heater on a slab over a heat sink: the surface temperature is P / (pi k) ln coth(pi x / (4 d)), and far away it decays as exp(-pi x / (2 d)).
# Reference: that closed form, within 3% (6% at the farthest probe) for a heater two cells wide.
title Line heater on a 6 um slab of conductivity 1.38
grid dx=0.125 dy=0.125
window width=96 ymin=-6 ymax=0
heater h xmin=-0.125 xmax=0.125 ymin=-0.125 ymax=0 power=0.1
probe p0 x=3.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p1 x=6.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p2 x=12.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p3 x=18.0625 y=-0.0625
expect response p0 h 222.734873 1e-7
expect response p1 h 95.6867339 1e-7
expect response p2 h 19.6248949 1e-7
expect response p3 h 4.07782149 1e-7
expect peak 102.511673 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 36864
expect response p0 h 222.757 0.03
expect response p1 h 95.6916 0.03
expect response p2 h 19.6237 0.03
expect response p3 h 4.07701 0.06
expect crosstalk p3 p2 h 0.20788 0.05
